<https://productencatalogus.data.vlaanderen.be/ns/ipdc-lpdc> a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Ontology>.
<https://productencatalogus.data.vlaanderen.be/ns/ipdc-lpdc#ConceptualPublicService> a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://productencatalogus.data.vlaanderen.be/ns/ipdc-lpdc>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The services provided by local authorities are often based on Flemish, federal or European legislation, which is translated to a local level. This means that the basis is the same for every local government, but that there may be flexibility for the local interpretation. Because we want to get and keep IPDC well stocked and up to date, with a limited administrative burden, we provide the concept. A draft is a template that editors of the Flemish government prepare for local authorities. It contains a general interpretation of a government service, which can also be applicable in most local contexts. Local authorities can consult these concepts and decide to register their own services on the basis of a concept. At that moment, a concept is cloned to an authority. The local government can then fully adapt this body and tailor it to the local context. In this way, a concept also groups together all the different local variations of a similar service."@en;
    <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/usageNote> "A good example of a concept is marriage. Although the description and conditions of a marriage are largely the same for the different municipalities, there may still be local differences, such as the location and price, which can be found in the respective authorities."@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status> <https://data.vlaanderen.be/id/concept/StandaardStatus/OntwerpStandaard>.
<https://productencatalogus.data.vlaanderen.be/ns/ipdc-lpdc#InstancePublicService> a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://productencatalogus.data.vlaanderen.be/ns/ipdc-lpdc>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Institutions are the actual interpretation of a product or service. The competent authority can vary: federal, Flemish, provincial,... And the service can be provided by another government such as a local government. A government service is a mandatory or optional set of activities that are or may be carried out by or on behalf of a public organisation, publicly funded and arising from public policy. Services may benefit an individual, an organisation or association, a company or other public authority, or groups of any of these parties. A service exists regardless of whether it is used or not. According to the revised European Interoperability Framework, a European public service includes any service provided by public authorities in Europe, or by other organisations on their behalf, to businesses, citizens or other public authorities."@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://purl.org/vocab/cpsv#PublicService>;
    <http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status> <https://data.vlaanderen.be/id/concept/StandaardStatus/OntwerpStandaard>.
<https://productencatalogus.data.vlaanderen.be/ns/ipdc-lpdc#FinancialAdvantage> a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://productencatalogus.data.vlaanderen.be/ns/ipdc-lpdc>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "We provide a subclass 'FinancialAdvantage' with 'Output'. This describes the premium amounts/subsidy amounts that are the result of the service."@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf> <http://data.europa.eu/m8g/Output>;
    <http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status> <https://data.vlaanderen.be/id/concept/StandaardStatus/OntwerpStandaard>.
<https://productencatalogus.data.vlaanderen.be/ns/ipdc-lpdc#ConceptualPublicServiceSnapshot> a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://productencatalogus.data.vlaanderen.be/ns/ipdc-lpdc>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A concept snapshot depicts what a concept looked like at a certain point in time. Each time a functional change is made, a new concept snapshot will be created. In this way, the complete editorial history of a concept is recorded."@en;
    <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/usageNote> "The concept snapshots are made available by IPDC on the basis of a linked data event stream (LDES). This LDES makes the full history of all concept changes available to connectors. More info about LDES is available here: https://semiceu.github.io/LinkedDataEventStreams"@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status> <https://data.vlaanderen.be/id/concept/StandaardStatus/OntwerpStandaard>.
<https://productencatalogus.data.vlaanderen.be/ns/ipdc-lpdc#InstancePublicServiceSnapshot> a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://productencatalogus.data.vlaanderen.be/ns/ipdc-lpdc>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "An instance snapshot shows what an instance looked like at a particular point in time. Each time a functional change is made, a new instance snapshot will be created. In this way, the complete editorial history of an instance is recorded."@en;
    <http://purl.org/vocab/vann/usageNote> "The instance data recordings are made available by IPDC using a linked data event stream (LDES). This LDES makes the full history of all instance changes available to connectors. More info about LDES is available here: https://semiceu.github.io/LinkedDataEventStreams"@en;
    <http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#status> <https://data.vlaanderen.be/id/concept/StandaardStatus/OntwerpStandaard>.
<https://productencatalogus.data.vlaanderen.be/ns/ipdc-lpdc#isArchived> a <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#DatatypeProperty>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy> <https://productencatalogus.data.vlaanderen.be/ns/ipdc-lpdc>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#domain> <https://productencatalogus.data.vlaanderen.be/ns/ipdc-lpdc#ConceptualPublicService>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#range> <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#boolean>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Value that indicates whether the draft is archived."@en;
